 note: in C++, they only set parent[i]=i for i=1..p-1, so parent[0] remains 0. So we'll do the same: parent = list(range(p)) gives parent[0]=0, parent[1]=1, etc. That's fine.\n        # However, we need to ensure that j is in range 0..p-1. Since (i*k)%p is already in that range.\n        # But in C++, they merge(i, (i*k)%p). If (i*k)%p == 0, they merge with 0. That's fine.\n        # So we can just use j as is.\n        nc = merge(parent, nc, i, j)\n\n    print(fmp(p, nc[0]))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-5.578839045483619e-05, -0.033102262765169144, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.16023385524749756, -0.0012668687850236893, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.00015877417172305286, -0.4773382246494293, 0.0, 0.0, -1.0967194612021558e-05, -0.0005980133428238332, -0.001503290724940598, -0.21518974006175995, -0.5771454572677612, -2.002696055569686e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.8596476365928538e-05, -9.536738616588991e-07, -0.12799499928951263, -0.06970354914665222, -0.025141878053545952, -9.536738616588991e-07, -5.94836674281396e-05, -1.5497195136049413e-06, -0.32021093368530273, -0.0005529781919904053, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -8.344646857949556e-07, -1.4305104514278355e-06, 0.0, -0.0002040654799202457, -5.960462772236497e-07, -1.311301275563892e-06, 0.0, -4.768370445162873e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -1.1920922133867862e-06, 0.0, -0.0031777145341038704, -4.768370445162873e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -3.6954811548639555e-06, -5.483612312673358e-06, -1.311301275563892e-06, -1.2993727978027891e-05, -0.0019350391812622547, -0.00017295771976932883, -0.0022953611332923174, -1.5497195136049413e-06, 0.0, -0.4218062162399292, -0.000974537746515125, -1.9073468138230965e-06, 0.0, 0.0, -4.291525328881107e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.0026530565228313208, -0.00033539868309162557, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-